The doctor examines me.
He takes his stethoscope.
"Please breathe in and out deeply," he says.
Then he shines a small lamp into my throat.
That is uncomfortable because my throat hurts so much.
"You have a heavy spring cold," the doctor confirms.
He looks at me seriously.
"You should sleep a lot now," he explains to me.
"And you should drink a lot of warm tea."
He also answers my question from earlier.
"No, you should absolutely not play badminton tomorrow," he says strictly.
"You are staying at home because you need rest."
I nod slowly.
I do not argue because I really do not feel well.
The doctor prints out a prescription for me.
He gives me the piece of paper.
It is a green prescription.
That means that I have to pay for this medicine myself at the pharmacy.
"Get well soon, Frau Flores," he says kindly.
I thank him and walk slowly to the door.
